  "description": "QOCJOK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C36 H78 Dy6 N12 O36,C36 H78 Dy6 N12 O36,6(C3 H7 N1 O1),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy7 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy8 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy9 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy5 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy6 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy10 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy11 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy12 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.714-3.743 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 108.75-111.51°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6(teaH)6(NO3)6]·3DMF·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)). Article name explicitly identifies Dy(III).",
